 "notes": "Kept all 5 old kinds and added City car (sourced to Wikipedia A-segment). Archetypes = model lines with generations as versions (Golf Mk1–Mk8, Corolla E210, Range Rover Classic/L322, Fiat 500 1957/2007, Mini/new Mini). Powertrain and size classes moved into t. Dropped from Saloon: Maybach S-Class and S-Class Saloon (go to Luxury saloon on the Luxury cars shelf); trimmed the Mercedes-heavy list to C-Class as an archetype plus A-Class Saloon and CLA as flat models. Mercedes V-Class/Viano/EQV kept as versions of a V-Class archetype sourced to the Vito article (no separate page retrieved, so no years). XPENG X9 left as a flat model (Wikipedia page not found). Range Rover Classic is also an off-roader; listed here per shelf brief, Off-roader shelf may cross-link. Brand entries use s=knowledge (country/founding only). No traditions apply. Golf Mk3–Mk6 years from their own Wikipedia pages."
